subproblem.statement:
Let n and l be natural numbers, mu a measure on R^(n+l), w : R^(n+l) -> R, y in R^(n+l), phi : R -> R, and R, eps, s, r real. Assume:
- eps > 0 and mu(B_R(y)) < infinity (closed ball);
- w is a.e.-strongly measurable for mu restricted to the open ball ball y R, and 0 <= w(x) <= 1 for mu-a.e. x in ball y R;
- phi is C^1 and nonincreasing, with phi(u) = 1 for u <= 1 and phi(u) = 0 for u >= 1 + eps;
- 0 < s <= r and (1 + eps) r < R.
Write r_x := |x - y|, phi' := deriv phi and Q(t) := -(integral (r_x/t) phi'(r_x/t) w(x) dmu)/t. Then the lower integral over closedBall y r minus ball y ((1+eps) s) of ofReal(w(x)/r_x^n) dmu is at most ofReal(integral_s^r Q(t)/t^n dt).
